    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (**45 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**).\n\n## What I changed\n\nOwner identity is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, with every derived value flowing from that new identity:\n\n1. **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 rewritten to build `<REGION>-<HASH8>` where `HASH8` is the first 8 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)`. The per-city sequence and the `OwnerRepository` dependency are gone \u2014 the code is now a stable function of who the owner is, not of how many owners exist.\n\n2. **`OwnerRegion.java`** (new) \u2014 the single source of truth for the REGION code: postcode range first (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099), then the fixed city table, else `UNKNOWN`. Shared by the customerCode and the locality.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.locality()`** \u2014 now derives locality from the region-and-hash identity (the REGION prefix of the `customerCode`), falling back to `OwnerRegion.of(owner)` for owners with no code (seed data). The old private `regionFromPostcode` helper was removed.\n\n4. **`membershipNumber` / `checkDigit` / audit record** \u2014 no code change needed; they already derive generically from `customerCode`, so they automatically carry the new identity (verified by Cp14, Cp31, Cp21).\n\n5. **Docs** \u2014 updated the `assignCode` step comment in `owners.POST.yml` and the `customerCode`/`locality` descriptions in `openapi.yml` to match the new design.\n\nOrdering holds: `ValidateOwnerFields` normalizes the telephone to E.164 and `ValidatePostcode`/`BuildOwner` set both fields on the entity before `assignCode` runs, so the hash input and region are exactly what the response reports back.",
